card.statement:
The Berezinian of $\Ymn$ is defined by

\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
B(u) = &\sum_{\sigma \in S_m} \sgn(\sigma) \, t_{\sigma(1)1}(u+\ga_1)t_{\sigma(2)2}(u+\ga_2)  \cdots t_{\sigma(m)m}(u+\ga_m)\\
&\times\sum_{\tau \in S_n} \sgn(\tau) \, t'_{m+1,m+\tau(1)}(u+\ga_{m+1}) \cdots t'_{m+n,m+\tau(n)}(u+\ga_{m+n}).
\end{split}
\end{equation}
